§ `The same word, defined differently by different codes (not a fork: each code is encoded as it states the list)`

-- Gov. Code § 17 names the firm; Civ. Code § 14(a) and Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(6) name the natural person and the corporation only.
#ASSERT `the term in the code names` "person" `in` `the Government Code` `the thing` "firm"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term in the code names` "person" `in` `the Civil Code` `the thing` "firm"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term in the code names` "person" `in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `the thing` "firm"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term in the code names` "person" `in` `the Government Code` `the thing` "natural person"
-- A term the deposit does not define in that code.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term in the code names` "sheriff" `in` `the Civil Code` `the thing` "marshal" BECAUSE "no deposited section of that code defines that term"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term in the code names` "writing" `in` `the Government Code` `the thing` "printing" BECAUSE "no deposited section of that code defines that term"
-- Real property is coextensive with lands, tenements and hereditaments in both codes; a definition by meaning is closed.
#ASSERT NOT (`the term in the code names` "real property" `in` `the Civil Code` `the thing` "money")

§ `Process: Gov. Code § 22 includes a writ or summons issued in judicial proceedings of a civil or criminal nature; Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7) signifies a writ or summons issued in a judicial proceeding`

#ASSERT `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` writ `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` TRUE `of the nature` `a proceeding of a civil nature`
#ASSERT `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` summons `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` TRUE `of the nature` `a proceeding of a civil nature`
#ASSERT `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` writ `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` TRUE `of the nature` `a proceeding of a criminal nature`
#ASSERT `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` summons `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` TRUE `of the nature` `a proceeding of a criminal nature`
#ASSERT REFUSED `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` writ `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` FALSE `of the nature` `a proceeding of a civil nature`
#ASSERT REFUSED `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` `some other document` `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` TRUE `of the nature` `a proceeding of a civil nature`
#ASSERT REFUSED `a document is process under Gov. Code § 22` writ `issued in the course of judicial proceedings:` TRUE `of the nature` `a proceeding of some other nature`
#ASSERT `a document is process under Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7)` writ `issued in the course of a judicial proceeding:` TRUE
#ASSERT `a document is process under Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7)` summons `issued in the course of a judicial proceeding:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a document is process under Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7)` writ `issued in the course of a judicial proceeding:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a document is process under Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(7)` `some other document` `issued in the course of a judicial proceeding:` TRUE)

§ `Testify and depose: Civ. Code § 14(a), Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(5)(A) and (B)`

#ASSERT `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Civil Code` testify `being` oral `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Civil Code` depose `being` written `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` testify `being` oral `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` depose `being` written `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE
-- Crossed pairings and a statement not under oath or affirmation: the sections do not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Civil Code` testify `being` written `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Civil Code` depose `being` oral `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` testify `being` oral `made under oath or affirmation:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` depose `being` written `made under oath or affirmation:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term embraces the statement, in` `the Government Code` testify `being` oral `made under oath or affirmation:` TRUE BECAUSE "the Government Code has no deposited section that defines testify or depose"

§ `Writ: Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(15) means an order or precept in writing, issued in the name of the people, or of a court or judicial officer`

#ASSERT `a document is a writ` TRUE TRUE `it is issued in` `the name of the people`
#ASSERT `a document is a writ` TRUE TRUE `it is issued in` `the name of a court`
#ASSERT `a document is a writ` TRUE TRUE `it is issued in` `the name of a judicial officer`
#ASSERT NOT (`a document is a writ` TRUE TRUE `it is issued in` `the name of someone else`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a document is a writ` FALSE TRUE `it is issued in` `the name of a court`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a document is a writ` TRUE FALSE `it is issued in` `the name of a court`)

§ `Affinity: Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(1)`

#ASSERT `a connection is affinity` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a connection is affinity` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a connection is affinity` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a connection is affinity` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Recycled water: Gov. Code § 26 borrows the meaning from Water Code § 13050(n), which is not deposited`

#ASSERT `the meaning in the Government Code of` "recycled water" `given that Water Code § 13050(n) defines recycled water as:` "the meaning X" EQUALS "the meaning X"
#ASSERT `the meaning in the Government Code of` "reclaimed water" `given that Water Code § 13050(n) defines recycled water as:` "the meaning X" EQUALS "the meaning X"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning in the Government Code of` "grey water" `given that Water Code § 13050(n) defines recycled water as:` "the meaning X"

§ `United States: Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(13)`

#ASSERT `the words United States may include` `the District of Columbia`
#ASSERT `the words United States may include` `the territories`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the words United States may include` `a state`

